---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---
<Layout title="About Morningwit" description="Morningwit is an independent site for small logic puzzles and gentle, layered hints. Here is how the puzzles are made and what the site does and does not do.">
	<div class="wrap-narrow prose">
		<h1>About Morningwit</h1>
		<p>
			Morningwit is a small, independent puzzle site. It has two jobs. The first is to give you logic puzzles you can play in a few quiet minutes.
			The second is to help when a daily word or number puzzle has you stuck, without handing you the answer before you want it.
		</p>

		<h2>How the puzzles are made</h2>
		<p>
			Every board on Morningwit is built by our own code. The generator makes a complete solution first, then removes clues one at a time. After each removal
			a solver checks that exactly one solution is left. If removing a clue would open up a second answer, the clue stays.
			Every board has exactly one answer. We also run a second solver that works the way a person does, and a board only ships if that solver can finish it with the same
			techniques the hints teach, so you never have to guess. On Binairo the difficulty setting controls how many clues you start with. On Star Battle the label tells you which technique the board needs.
		</p>
		<p>
			The daily puzzle is built from the date, so everyone who opens it on the same day gets the same board. You do not need an account, and there is no leaderboard.
		</p>

		<h2>What we keep, and what we do not</h2>
		<p>
			Your progress, timer setting and streak live in your own browser. We do not ask you to sign up, and the boards you play are not sent anywhere.
			Details are on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Hints for other puzzles</h2>
		<p>
			Hints for well-known daily puzzles follow the same rule as our own games: a nudge first, the reasoning second, the answer last.
			Read <a href="/fair-hints/">how hints work</a> for the details.
		</p>

		<div class="note">
			Morningwit is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to The New York Times or any other puzzle publisher. Game names such as Connections, Strands,
			Spelling Bee, Letter Boxed and Wordle belong to their owners. We use those names only to say which puzzle a hint is about.
		</div>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Found a bug, a board that felt unfair, or a hint that gave too much away? Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
